 "answer": "To configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model globally, ensuring that OpenAI is never contacted, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Install the Required Packages**: Ensure you have the necessary integration packages for Ollama and Hugging Face.\n\n2. **Set the Global Embedding Model**: Use the `Settings` object to specify the global default embedding model, which will be a Hugging Face model.\n\n3. **Set Up the Local Ollama LLM**: Configure the LlamaIndex to use Ollama as the local LLM.\n\nHere's how you can achieve this:\n\n### Step-by-Step Configuration\n\n1. **Install the Packages**:\n   Ensure you have the following packages installed:\n   - `llama-index-embeddings-huggingface` for Hugging Face embeddings.\n   - `llama-index-llms-ollama` for Ollama integration.\n\n   You can install them using pip:\n   ```bash\n   pip install llama-index-embeddings-huggingface llama-index-llms-ollama\n   ```\n\n2. **Set Up the Global Embedding Model**:\n   Use the `Settings` object to set the global default embedding model to a Hugging Face model.\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   # Set the global default embedding model to a Hugging Face model\n   Settings.embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding(model_name=\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")\n   ```\n\n   This configuration uses the `HuggingFaceEmbedding` class to specify the embedding model globally. The model name `\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"` is an example and can be replaced with any other Hugging Face model as needed.\n\n3. **Configure the Local Ollama LLM**:\n   Set up the Ollama LLM to run locally.\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\n\n   # Configure the Ollama LLM\n   llm = Ollama(\n       model=\"llama3.3\",\n       request_timeout=60.0,\n       context_window=8000,  # Optionally set the context window\n   )\n   ```\n\n   This snippet configures Ollama to use the model `llama3.3` with a specified request timeout and context window.\n\n### References\n\n- The global embedding model configuration is described in the context:\n  > \"changing the global default `Settings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding()`\" [6] llama_index/docs/src/content/docs/framework/module_guides/models/embeddings.md (lines 40-45)\n\n- The setup for using a local Ollama LLM is detailed here:\n  > \"if you have [Ollama](https://github.com/ollama/ollama) installed and running\" [7] llama_index/docs/src/content/docs/framework/understanding/using_llms.md (lines 153-168)\n\nBy following these steps, you ensure that LlamaIndex uses a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model globally, without contacting OpenAI.",
